  "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+4 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-5x-10\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x-12}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}-5x-10$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder $2.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-5x-10}{x-3}=3x+4+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$",
